// triangle's own depth slope per pixel, i.e. it grows with the viewing angle: at oblique / grazing views it pulled a
// layer 1-40 cm forward, so a wall, trim or floor BEHIND the surface in view (the next room's wall, the floor under a
// slab, the wall behind a poster / graffiti card / crate face, the far face of a thick wall) won the depth test and was
// drawn over it (work/test_map_vanish.cjs: 0.5-1% of all surface pixels on every map). Layers now use the units term
// only: NM_ZBIAS depth steps per level, a constant number of depth-buffer steps whatever the angle (a few tenths of a
